At 06:48 AM 2/4/03 -0500, Pierre wrote:
>How would you lex the following?:

My best guess, and I'm not using any algorithm per se.

>/la xidEkel. rIrxe fa'o tIgri se li ni stIka lI te/
                         # and abort processing at this point.

I insert the apparent comma without which the following isn't a proper 
speech stream.

>/la xidEkel. rIrxefa'o,elinistIkalItetIgris/

If there is a word break there, then the same termination takes place.

A long name with many false stresses marked, so it is still invalid because 
of more than one stress per word.

>/mi dUnda le cUkta la fa'oz/

